Five of the six pictures in this directory are NOT under the repository's MIT licence.
======================================================================================

    fixture-intro.png
    fixture-sentence.png
    paint-vocabulary.png
    mask-under-transform.png
    mask-explicit-rect.png

Each of these composites the photography, the channel logo, or both, from
fixtures/en-halloween-decorating/ -- which is "all rights reserved" media, not MIT. A
render of copyrighted media is a derivative of it, so these five carry the same terms:

    Copyright (c) 2026 Mohammad Bagher Ehtemam. All rights reserved. Permission is
    granted to use these files ONLY to build, test, benchmark and study this repository.
    Any other use requires the copyright holder's written permission.

text-features.png draws only text, on a blank ground, with no channel media in it. It is
MIT along with the rest of the code.

The canonical list of every carved-out path in the tree is ../../../../LICENSE-MEDIA.md.


Why these five do not ship to crates.io
---------------------------------------

A crate's `license = "MIT"` field is a machine-readable claim over every byte in its
tarball, and for these five that claim would be false. They are therefore listed in
`exclude` in ../../Cargo.toml. Nothing is lost by it: the tests that read them also read
the fixture through ../../../../fixtures/, which is outside the crate, so they already
cannot run from a published tarball. text-features.png is not excluded.

A golden added here that draws any of the fixture's media must be added to the exclude
list and to LICENSE-MEDIA.md at the same time.
